<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Transcaucasian Commissariat</h1><p class="st-meta">1917 CE – 1918 CE · capital Tiflis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first regional government of Transcaucasia after the October Revolution, which refused to recognise Bolshevik power and paved the way for independence.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Bolsheviks</a> seized power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a> in November 1917, Georgian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mensheviks">Mensheviks</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenian-revolutionary-federation">Armenian Dashnaks</a> and Azerbaijani <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musavat">Musavatists</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tiflis</a> refused to accept their rule. On 28 November 1917 they formed the Transcaucasian Commissariat as a provisional government for the region, splitting from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/russian-republic">Russian Republic</a> in practice.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Chaired by the Georgian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mensheviks">Menshevik</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evgeni-gegechkori">Evgeni Gegechkori</a>, it was a coalition of the three main national parties. It signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzincan">Erzincan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> in December 1917 as the Russian army melted away from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> front, and faced rising ethnic violence and food shortages. In February 1918 it convened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transcaucasian-sejm">Transcaucasian Sejm</a> from deputies elected to the Russian Constituent Assembly.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under pressure from Ottoman advances and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-brest-litovsk">Treaty of Brest-Litovsk</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a> declared independence in April 1918, replacing the Commissariat with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/transcaucasian-democratic-federative-republic">Transcaucasian Democratic Federative Republic</a>. Its brief life marked the first step from Russian rule towards the separate republics of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/georgia">Georgia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/transcaucasian-commissariat.jpg" alt="Transcaucasian Commissariat" width="320" height="216"><figcaption>Image: Russian Tzar Ministry of Internal Affairs · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map-1903-caucasus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1917 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tiflis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Evgeni Gegechkori</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian; Georgian; Armenian; Azerbaijani</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a>, <a href="/countries/armenia">Armenia</a>, <a href="/countries/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Zakavkom, Transcaucasian Sejm government</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=transcaucasian-commissariat" aria-label="Transcaucasian Commissariat on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5772 692 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Transcaucasian Commissariat lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6092 948L5635 424M6092 948L6089 946"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5635 424h0M6089 946h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6092 948h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6092 948h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tiflis. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=transcaucasian-commissariat">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
